# Three.js skills (cloudai-x/threejs-skills)

Targets **three@0.186** (r186), React Three Fiber 9.8, drei 10.7, gltf-transform 4.5.

Load **one** topic skill from `.cursor/skills/threejs-<topic>/SKILL.md` based on the task (descriptions in each file’s frontmatter). Do not load all thirteen for every request.

| Task | Skill |
| --- | --- |
| New scene, camera, renderer, loop | `threejs-fundamentals` |
| Meshes, BufferGeometry, instancing | `threejs-geometry` |
| Materials, PBR, nodes | `threejs-materials` |
| Lights, shadows, HDR | `threejs-lighting` |
| Textures, color space, RTT | `threejs-textures` |
| Keyframes, skinning, morphs | `threejs-animation` |
| glTF / Draco / KTX2 loading | `threejs-loaders` |
| Shaders, TSL | `threejs-shaders` |
| PostFX, EffectComposer | `threejs-postprocessing` |
| Raycast, controls, gizmos | `threejs-interaction` |
| Profiling, draw calls, memory | `threejs-performance` |
| React Three Fiber + drei | `threejs-react-three-fiber` |
| gltf-transform CLI pipeline | `threejs-asset-pipeline` |

Prefer **Common Mistakes** sections in each skill over outdated training-data APIs (`RGBELoader`, legacy `Clock`, etc.).

For 3D UI polish on Apple or web surfaces, coordinate with `ui-ux-skills-coordination.mdc` after the scene runs correctly.
